"""USBLC6-2SC6 - two-line very low capacitance ESD protection with a rail clamp, SOT23-6L. Bare part.

Datasheet: ST USBLC6-2, DocID 11265 Rev 5 (October 2011).

Pins (Figure 1, top view): 1 I/O1, 2 GND, 3 I/O2, 4 I/O2, 5 VBUS, 6 I/O1. Each line passes
through the package: pads 1 and 6 are the same line (I/O1), pads 3 and 4 the other (I/O2).

Topology (section 2.1, Figure 6): rail to rail. Each I/O has a steering diode to the VBUS pin
and one to GND, and a transil clamps the VBUS pin to GND. A positive surge on an I/O is clamped
at VTRANSIL + VF, a negative one at -VF. The VBUS pin connects to the protected circuit's supply
(section 2.2, "the connections from the pin VBUS to VCC"); an I/O that rises a diode drop above
that supply conducts into it.

Ratings (Table 1, p2): IEC 61000-4-2 15 kV air and 15 kV contact discharge; Tj -40 to 125 C.
Electrical characteristics (Table 2, Tamb 25 C): leakage IRM 10 / 150 nA at VRM 5.25 V;
breakdown VBUS to GND 6 V min at 1 mA; VF 1.1 V max at 10 mA; clamping, any I/O to GND, 12 V at
IPP 1 A and 17 V at 5 A (8/20 us); capacitance I/O to GND 2.5 / 3.5 pF and I/O to I/O 1.2 /
1.7 pF at VR 1.65 V.

Layout (section 2.3): the tracks from the lines to the I/O pins, from the supply to VBUS and
from GND to the GND pin must be as short as possible; the part sits at the connector.

The component type is "esd", so board checks find it as the ESD protection of its lines.
"""

# Table 2: the leakage is specified up to VRM 5.25 V on the VBUS rail.
VBUS = io(Power(voltage="0V to 5.25V"))
GND = io(Ground)
IO1 = io(Net)
IO2 = io(Net)

Component(
    name="USBLC6",
    prefix="U",
    symbol=Symbol(library="USBLC6-2SC6.kicad_sym"),
    footprint=File("SOT-23-6_ST_USBLC6-2SC6.kicad_mod"),
    part=Part(mpn="USBLC6-2SC6", manufacturer="STMicroelectronics"),
    type="esd",
    pins={
        "I/O1": IO1,
        "GND": GND,
        "I/O2": IO2,
        "VBUS": VBUS,
    },
)
